# 10. Barcode Types

The system should support configurable barcode formats.

Common formats:

```text
CODE_128
CODE_39
EAN_13
EAN_8
UPC_A
UPC_E
ITF_14
GS1_128
GS1_DATA_MATRIX
QR_CODE
```

Do not claim that every format is interchangeable.

For retail products, EAN/UPC/GTIN identifiers may need to follow appropriate GS1 rules.

For internal warehouse/POS labels, CODE_128 is often a practical choice.

---

# 11. Barcode Modes

Product creation MUST support:

```text
Barcode

○ Generate Automatically
○ Enter Existing Barcode
○ Generate From SKU
○ Add Multiple Barcodes
○ No Barcode
```

Example:

```text
Barcode Type:
[ CODE_128 ]

Barcode:
[ Generate ]

SKU:
TSH-OVR-BLK-M

[ Generate Barcode ]
```

---

# 12. Generate Barcode From SKU

The platform MAY generate an internal barcode representing the SKU.

Example:

```text
SKU:

TSH-OVR-BLK-M

↓

CODE_128

↓

████████████████
████ ███ ███████
████████████████

Human-readable:
TSH-OVR-BLK-M
```

Important:

A generated internal CODE_128 barcode is NOT automatically a globally registered retail GTIN/EAN/UPC.

Do not present internally generated barcodes as globally unique GS1 identifiers.

---

# 13. Existing Barcode Entry

Merchants may already have manufacturer barcodes.

Product creation:

```text
Barcode Mode:
[ Existing Barcode ]

Barcode:
[ 8901234567890 ]

Type:
[ EAN-13 ]
```

Validate:

* Format
* Length
* Check digit where applicable
* Duplicate barcode
* Status
* Scope
* Assignment

