# 38. Security

Never trust:

```text
storeId
vendorId
productId
variantId
```

from the frontend.

Every identifier operation MUST validate:

```text
Authenticated user
↓
Platform access
↓
Vendor access
↓
Store access
↓
Product access
↓
Variant access
```

Prevent IDOR attacks.

Vendor A MUST NOT be able to resolve or modify Vendor B's private catalog through SKU/barcode manipulation.

---

# 39. Store Scope

Because the platform is multi-vendor and multi-store:

```text
Platform
 ├── Vendor A
 │    ├── Store A1
 │    └── Store A2
 │
 └── Vendor B
      └── Store B1
```

Determine identifier scope from the Catalog architecture.

If SKU is store-scoped:

```text
(storeId, sku)
```

If platform/vendor scoped:

```text
(platformId, sku)
```

Do not introduce a conflicting uniqueness rule without checking the existing Catalog model.

